      "content": "Switching from `fmt.Fprint` to `fmt.Fprintln` changes the spacing semantics. `Fprint` only inserts spaces between operands when neither is a string, so the original produced `build starting at <time>` (no space before time since the preceding operand is a string). `Fprintln` always inserts spaces between all operands, so this now produces `build starting at  <time>` (double space, since there was already a trailing space in the literal). Remove the trailing space in the string literal, e.g. `\"build starting at\"`, to preserve intended formatting."
